              THE SERVICE IS PROVIDED ON AN "AS IS" AND "AS AVAILABLE" BASIS, WITHOUT WARRANTIES OF ANY KIND, EITHER EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, NON-INFRINGEMENT, RELIABILITY, ACCURACY, OR COMPLETENESS.
            </p>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-3">
            We do not warrant that:
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-6">
            <li>The Service will be uninterrupted, timely, secure, or error-free;</li>
            <li>Backup files will be free from corruption, complete, or suitable for restoration in all circumstances;</li>
            <li>The Service will meet your specific requirements or achieve any particular outcome;</li>
            <li>Any defects or errors in the Service will be corrected within any specific timeframe.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <%# ── 4. Client Responsibilities ─────────────────────── %>
        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">4. Client Responsibilities</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            You acknowledge and agree that you bear <strong>sole responsibility</strong> for:
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-6">
            <li><strong>Database credentials and access:</strong> Safeguarding all database connection credentials you provide to the Service. You must use credentials with the minimum privileges necessary.</li>
            <li><strong>Backup verification:</strong> Periodically testing that your backups are complete, valid, and restorable. DataKeep automates the process; you must verify the outcome.</li>
            <li><strong>Retention and compliance:</strong> Configuring retention policies that meet your legal, regulatory, and business requirements (e.g., GDPR, HIPAA, PCI-DSS, SOX).</li>
            <li><strong>Encryption and security:</strong> Deciding whether to enable encryption for backups at rest. When encryption is disabled, backup files are stored in plaintext.</li>
            <li><strong>Storage backend security:</strong> Ensuring that any storage destination you configure (your own S3 buckets, local servers, etc.) is properly secured, access-controlled, and compliant with applicable regulations.</li>
            <li><strong>Network and VPN configuration:</strong> Providing correct VPN and network settings. DataKeep is not responsible for connectivity failures, misconfigured tunnels, or firewall rules.</li>
            <li><strong>Data ownership:</strong> You are the sole owner of your data. We do not claim any rights to data that passes through or is stored via the Service.</li>
            <li><strong>Disaster recovery planning:</strong> Maintaining your own disaster recovery plan. DataKeep is one component of a backup strategy, not a substitute for a comprehensive DR plan.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <%# ── 5. Data Processing ─────────────────────────────── %>
        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">5. Data Processing and Handling</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            When performing backup, sync, or restore operations, your database data passes through our infrastructure transiently. We:
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-6">
            <li><strong>Do not inspect, analyze, mine, or monetize</strong> your backup data under any circumstances;</li>
            <li><strong>Do not retain</strong> transient copies beyond what is necessary to complete the requested operation;</li>
            <li>Encrypt backup files using AES-256-GCM when you enable the encryption option;</li>
            <li>Store encryption keys using application-level encryption (Active Record Encryption) — keys are never stored in plaintext;</li>
            <li>Delete temporary files immediately after upload to your configured storage backends.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

